st of those code execution bugs are memory errors or type confusion, where PostgreSQL handles a value as the wrong data type. They turn up in PL/Perl and PL/Tcl, text search functions such as ts_rank_cd(), parallel query, logical replication, dblink and statistics import. Thirty-two of the 52 CVEs carry … More → The post PostgreSQL security update fixes 52 vulnerabilities, ends support for PostgreSQL 14 appeared first</description><chr2:heatScore>65.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>GMO事件“情報漏えい”だけでは済まない…FX不正取引も起きた攻撃の「本当の深刻さ」</title><link>https://www.sbbit.jp/article/fj/187797?ref=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:41a16cce0dd898d69f6ab3ba68aa21f8e94d68df587281843939e105c394eae4</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>Business+IT Hot Topics Filtered</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-13T08:07:22.787188+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>「身に覚えのないFX取引」が現実に起きた──。9月から10月に相次いだ不正アクセス事件の中でも、GMOインターネットの「お名前.com デスクトップクラウド」を襲った攻撃は深刻だ。取引口座の認証情報が不正利用されたうえ、攻撃者はGMOに金銭を要求し、顧客情報の公開やランサムウェア攻撃まで予告。GMOはついに政府へ「能動的サイバー防御」の適用を緊急要請した。サイバー攻撃を企業だけで防ぐ時代は、限界を迎えつつあるのか。</description><chr2:heatScore>65.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>New worm-like 'SCKit' malware targets MSPs in ScreenConnect attacks</title><link>https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-worm-like-sckit-malware-targets-msps-in-screenconnect-attacks/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:afe79ee14497cedd484f32970a07fb09e3d9cfc073cca58ae8f80bd228f3726c</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>BleepingComputer</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-13T08:07:21.535044+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:53:10 GMT</pubDate><description>A new worm-like malware toolkit named SCKit was deployed in the recent ScreenConnect attacks targeting managed service providers (MSPs), designed to spread from infected customer devices to MSP technicians' computers and compromise additional managed networks. [...]</description><chr2:heatScore>65.0</chr2:heatScore></item></channel></rss>